srow(318, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'"THEY SACRIFICED TO DEMONS, NO-GODS" (32:17) — HAD THEY SERVED THE SUN AND THE MOON, THE STARS AND THE CONSTELLATIONS, THINGS THE WORLD NEEDS AND BENEFITS BY, THE JEALOUSY WOULD NOT BE DOUBLED; BUT THEY SERVE THINGS THAT DO THEM NO GOOD BUT HARM. "TO DEMONS" — WHAT IS A DEMON\'S WAY? IT ENTERS A MAN AND OVERPOWERS HIM. ({SP_(318, 13, "לא", "היתה", "קנאה", "כפולה")} "the jealousy would not be doubled"; {SP_(318, 13, "מה", "דרכו", "של", "שד")} "what is a demon\'s way"; {SP_(318, 13, "נכנס", "באדם", "וכופה", "אותו")} "it enters a man and overpowers him"): the doubled jealousy (Onkelos\'s "demons in whom is no use" — the measure — the spine\'s "things that harm them"); the Sifra on Leviticus 17:7 the parallel, cited; no law (DV32-06). Fresh.')
srow(318, 14, 'MATERIAL', f'"GODS THEY KNEW NOT" — WHOM THE NATIONS OF THE WORLD DO NOT RECOGNIZE; "NEW ONES THAT CAME UP OF LATE" — WHENEVER ONE OF THE NATIONS SEES IT HE SAYS: THIS IS A JEWISH IMAGE; "AS MY HAND HAS FOUND THE KINGDOMS OF THE IDOLS, WHOSE IMAGES EXCEEDED JERUSALEM\'S AND SAMARIA\'S" (Isaiah 10:10) — IT TEACHES THAT JERUSALEM AND SAMARIA SUPPLIED THE MOLD FOR ALL WHO COME INTO THE WORLD. ({SP_(318, 14, "שאין", "אמות", "העולם", "מכירים", "אותם")} "whom the nations of the world do not recognize"; {SP_(318, 14, "צלם", "יהודים", "הוא", "זה")} "this is a Jewish image"): the new gods Israel\'s own inventions (the Prophets\' seat cited, never read); no law (DV32-06). Fresh.')
srow(318, 15, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHICH YOUR FATHERS DREADED NOT" — THE HAIR OF YOUR FATHERS DID NOT STAND UP BEFORE THEM; ANOTHER WORD: YOUR FATHERS DID NOT INQUIRE TO KNOW WHETHER THERE IS ANY USE IN THEM OR NOT. ({SP_(318, 15, "שלא", "עמדה", "שערת", "אבותיכם", "בפניהם")} "the hair of your fathers did not stand up before them"; {SP_(318, 15, "לידע", "אם", "יש", "בהם", "צרך", "אם", "לאו")} "to know whether there is use in them or not"): se\'arum read by the hair (se\'ar) and by inquiry; the English misprints the verse (32:18 for 32:17\'s words); no law (DV32-06). Fresh.')
srow(318, 16, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "WHICH YOUR FATHERS DREADED NOT" — DO NOT READ "YOUR FATHERS DREADED THEM NOT" BUT "YOUR FATHERS REGARDED THEM NOT": THOUGH THEY SACRIFICED AND BURNED INCENSE TO THEM THEY DID NOT FEAR THEM, AS IT SAYS "BUT TO CAIN AND HIS OFFERING HE HAD NO REGARD" (Genesis 4:5). ({SP_(318, 16, "אל", "תהי", "קורא")} "do not read"; {SP_(318, 16, "אלא", "לא", "שעום", "אבתיכם")} "but: your fathers regarded them not"; {SP_(318, 16, "לא", "היו", "יראים", "מהם")} "they did not fear them"): the second "do not read" — sha\'u (regarded) for se\'arum (dreaded), Genesis 4:5\'s Cain the seat that read this row at the Genesis ledger of Cain and Abel (a RUN CITATION of the tape\'s own entry); the compile: no law (DV32-06). REREAD WHOLE (the Genesis ledger gen_12_cain_abel\'s reading — Genesis 4:5).')
srow(319, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"OF THE ROCK THAT BEGOT YOU YOU WERE UNMINDFUL" (32:18) — THE HOLY ONE SAID TO THEM: YOU HAVE MADE ME AS A MALE SEEKING TO GIVE BIRTH: WERE A WOMAN SITTING ON THE BIRTHSTOOL WOULD SHE NOT BE IN PAIN — "THE CHILDREN ARE COME TO THE BIRTH AND THERE IS NO STRENGTH TO BRING FORTH" (2 Kings 19:3)? WERE SHE IN LABOR WITH HER FIRSTBORN — "I HAVE HEARD A VOICE AS OF A WOMAN IN TRAVAIL, THE ANGUISH AS OF HER THAT BRINGS FORTH HER FIRST CHILD" (Jeremiah 4:31)? WERE THERE TWO IN HER WOMB — "AND THE CHILDREN STRUGGLED WITHIN HER" (Genesis 25:22)? WERE IT A MALE, WHOSE WAY IS NOT TO BEAR, SEEKING TO BEAR — WOULD THE PAIN NOT BE DOUBLED AND REDOUBLED — "ASK NOW AND SEE WHETHER A MAN TRAVAILS WITH CHILD" (Jeremiah 30:6)? The head row of piska 319 ({SP_(319, 1, "עשיתם", "אותי", "כאלו", "אני", "זכר", "מבקש", "לילד")} "you have made Me as a male seeking to give birth"; {SP_(319, 1, "לא", "היה", "צער", "כפול", "ומכפל")} "would the pain not be doubled and redoubled"): THE ROCK THAT BEGOT read by the pains of birth in four degrees (the a-fortiori of pains, I1); Genesis 25:22\'s twins the tape\'s own entry (a RUN CITATION); the English misprints Jeremiah 4:13 for 4:31; the Prophets\' seats cited, never read; no law (DV32-06). Fresh.')
srow(319, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"OF THE ROCK THAT BEGOT YOU YOU WERE UNMINDFUL" — YOU FORGOT ME BY THE MERIT OF YOUR FATHERS: "LOOK TO THE ROCK FROM WHICH YOU WERE HEWN AND TO THE HOLE OF THE PIT FROM WHICH YOU WERE DUG" (Isaiah 51:1). ({SP_(319, 2, "שכחתם", "אותי", "בזכות", "אבותיכם")} "you forgot Me by the merit of your fathers"): the Rock the fathers (Isaiah 51:1-2 — Abraham the rock hewn from; the Prophets\' seat cited, never read); the syntax disputed by the translators (Basser, Hammer); no law (DV32-06). Fresh.')
srow(319, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "OF THE ROCK THAT BEGOT YOU YOU WERE UNMINDFUL (teshi)" — WHENEVER I SEEK TO DO YOU GOOD YOU WEAKEN (matishim) THE POWER ABOVE: YOU STOOD AT THE SEA AND SAID "THIS IS MY GOD AND I WILL GLORIFY HIM" (Exodus 15:2) — I SOUGHT TO DO YOU GOOD, AND YOU TURNED AND SAID "LET US MAKE A CAPTAIN AND RETURN TO EGYPT" (Numbers 14:4); YOU STOOD BEFORE MOUNT SINAI AND SAID "ALL THAT THE LORD HAS SPOKEN WE WILL DO AND HEAR" (Exodus 24:7) — I SOUGHT TO DO YOU GOOD, AND YOU TURNED AND SAID TO THE CALF "THESE ARE YOUR GODS, O ISRAEL" (Exodus 32:4). ({SP_(319, 3, "אתם", "מתישים", "כח", "של", "מעלה")} "you weaken the Power above"; {SP_(319, 3, "בקשתי", "להיטיב", "לכם", "חזרתם", "בכם")} "I sought to do you good — you turned back"): THE POWER WEAKENED — the two promises and the two reversals (the sea and the spies, Sinai and the calf — the tape\'s own entries, RUN CITATIONS); the English misprints Genesis 15:2 for Exodus 15:2; the seat that read this row at the Genesis ledger of the covenant of the pieces; no law (DV32-06). REREAD WHOLE (the Genesis ledger gen_31_covenant_pieces\' reading).')
srow(319, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU FORGOT GOD WHO BORE YOU (mecholelekha)" — R. MEIR SAYS: THE GOD WHO TRAVAILED WITH YOU, WHO WAS PAINED FOR YOU — "PAIN AS OF A WOMAN IN TRAVAIL" (Psalm 48:7); R. YEHUDAH SAYS: WHO MADE YOU HOLLOWS UPON HOLLOWS. ({SP_(319, 4, "אל", "שהחיל", "בך", "אל", "שנצטער", "בך")} "the God who travailed with you, the God who was pained for you"; {SP_(319, 4, "שעשך", "מחילים", "מחילים")} "who made you hollows upon hollows"): the verb\'s root (ch-l — travail, hollow) two ways; the Writings\' seat cited, never read; no law (DV32-06). Fresh.')
srow(319, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "AND YOU FORGOT GOD WHO BORE YOU" — THE GOD WHO MADE HIS NAME REST (hechil) UPON YOU AS ON NO NATION OR KINGDOM: "I AM THE LORD YOUR GOD WHO BROUGHT YOU OUT OF THE LAND OF EGYPT" (Exodus 20:2); R. NEHEMIAH SAYS: THE GOD WHO MAKES YOU SICK (cholim) BEFORE ALL WHO COME INTO THE WORLD WHEN YOU DO NOT DO THE TORAH — "THE VOICE OF THE LORD IS UPON THE WATERS" TO "THE VOICE OF THE LORD MAKES THE HINDS TRAVAIL" (Psalm 29:3-9). ({SP_(319, 5, "אל", "שהחיל", "שמו", "עליך")} "the God who made His Name rest upon you"; {SP_(319, 5, "אל", "עשך", "חולים", "על", "כל", "באי", "העולם")} "the God who makes you sick before all who come into the world"): the Name resting (Exodus 20:2 the tape\'s own entry — a RUN CITATION) and the sickness before the nations; the Writings\' seat cited, never read; no law (DV32-06). Fresh.')
srow(319, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "AND YOU FORGOT GOD WHO BORE YOU" — THE GOD WHO FORGIVES (mochel) YOU ALL YOUR INIQUITIES. ({SP_(319, 6, "אל", "שמוחל", "לך", "על", "כל", "עונותיך")} "the God who forgives you all your iniquities"): the last row of the piska — the verb by assonance alone (the translator); no law (DV32-06). Fresh.')
srow(320, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE LORD SAW AND SPURNED" (32:19) — R. YEHUDAH SAYS: FROM WHAT HE GAVE THEM OF HIS OWN (hin\'am) THEY SPURN (mena\'atzim) BEFORE HIM. The head row of piska 320 ({SP_(320, 1, "ממה", "שהנאם", "משלו", "מנאצים", "לפניו")} "from what He gave them of His own they spurn before Him"): the spurning made of the gift (the pun the translator names); no law (DV32-07). Fresh.')
srow(320, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'R. MEIR SAYS: "BECAUSE OF THE PROVOKING OF HIS SONS AND HIS DAUGHTERS" — AND IS IT NOT AN A-FORTIORI: IF WHEN THEY PROVOKE THEY ARE CALLED CHILDREN, HAD THEY NOT PROVOKED, HOW MUCH MORE. ({SP_(320, 2, "מכעיס", "בניו", "ובנותיו")} "the provoking of His sons and His daughters"; {SP_(320, 2, "ומה", "בזמן", "שמכעיסים", "קרויים", "בנים")} "if when they provoke they are called children"): R. Meir\'s sonship argument again (308:1\'s form, I1); no law (DV32-07). Fresh.')
srow(320, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE SAID: I WILL HIDE MY FACE FROM THEM" (32:20) — THE HOLY ONE SAID: BEHOLD, I REMOVE MY SHEKHINAH FROM AMONG THEM; "I WILL SEE WHAT THEIR END SHALL BE" — AND I WILL KNOW WHAT THEIR END IS. ({SP_(320, 3, "הריני", "מסלק", "שכינתי", "מביניהם")} "behold, I remove My Shekhinah from among them"): ONKELOS\'S WORDS IN THE SPINE — "I will remove My Shekhinah" is the Aramaic of 32:20 (asalek shekhinti — the measure) and the Hebrew of this row: the translator and the spine one reading of the hidden face (31:17-18\'s rendering too); the compile: the face_hidden effect (31:17 on the tape) seated in the song (DV32-07). Fresh.')
srow(320, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: BEHOLD, I HAND THEM OVER INTO THE HAND OF THE FOUR KINGDOMS THAT THEY MAY ENSLAVE THEM. ({SP_(320, 4, "הריני", "מוסרם", "ביד", "ארבע", "מלכיות")} "behold, I hand them over into the hand of the four kingdoms"): the hiding as the handing over (the four kingdoms — 313:15, 317:4); no law (DV32-07). Fresh.')
srow(320, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"I WILL SEE WHAT THEIR END SHALL BE" — I WILL KNOW WHAT THEIR END IS; "FOR THEY ARE A GENERATION OF OVERTURNINGS (tahpukhot)" — AN OVERTURNED GENERATION; NOT "A GENERATION THAT OVERTURNS" IS WRITTEN BUT "A GENERATION OF OVERTURNINGS": THEY ARE FICKLE, THEY ARE FAITHLESS. ({SP_(320, 5, "דור", "תהפך", "אין", "כתוב", "כאן", "אלא")} "a generation that overturns is not written here but"; {SP_(320, 5, "הפכפכנים", "הם", "פורנים", "הם")} "they are fickle, they are faithless"): the noun\'s plural read as habit; no law (DV32-07). Fresh.')
srow(320, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"CHILDREN IN WHOM IS NO FAITHFULNESS" — YOU ARE CHILDREN IN WHOM THERE IS NO FAITH: YOU STOOD AT MOUNT SINAI AND SAID "ALL THAT THE LORD HAS SPOKEN WE WILL DO AND HEAR" (Exodus 24:7), AND I SAID "YOU ARE GODS" (Psalm 82:6); WHEN YOU SAID TO THE CALF "THESE ARE YOUR GODS, O ISRAEL" (Exodus 32:4), I SAID TO YOU "SURELY AS MAN YOU SHALL DIE" (Psalm 82:7); I BROUGHT YOU INTO THE LAND OF YOUR FATHERS AND BUILT YOU THE CHOSEN HOUSE AND SAID YOU WOULD NEVER BE EXILED FROM IT; WHEN YOU SAID "WE HAVE NO PORTION IN DAVID" (2 Samuel 20:1), I SAID "ISRAEL SHALL SURELY BE LED CAPTIVE OUT OF HIS LAND" (Amos 7:17). R. DOSTAI BEN YEHUDAH SAYS: DO NOT READ "NO FAITHFULNESS (emun) IN THEM" BUT "NO AMEN IN THEM" — THEY WOULD NOT ANSWER AMEN AFTER THE PROPHETS WHEN THEY BLESSED THEM: "TO PERFORM THE OATH WHICH I SWORE TO YOUR FATHERS, TO GIVE THEM A LAND FLOWING WITH MILK AND HONEY, AS THIS DAY" (Jeremiah 11:5) — AND NOT ONE OPENED HIS MOUTH TO ANSWER AMEN UNTIL JEREMIAH CAME AND ANSWERED: "AND I ANSWERED AND SAID: AMEN, O LORD". ({SP_(320, 6, "בנים", "אתם", "שאין", "בכם", "אמונה")} "you are children in whom there is no faith"; {SP_(320, 6, "כיון", "שאמרתם", "לעגל")} "when you said to the calf"; {SP_(320, 6, "אל", "תהי", "קורא", "לא", "אמן", "בם")} "do not read: no faithfulness in them, but no Amen in them"; {SP_(320, 6, "עד", "שבא", "ירמיה", "וענה", "אמן")} "until Jeremiah came and answered Amen"): TWO FORFEITS — Sinai\'s "you are gods" lost at the calf, the Temple\'s permanence lost at "no portion in David" (the tape\'s own entries Exodus 24:7, 32:4 RUN CITATIONS; the Prophets\' and the Writings\' seats cited); R. DOSTAI\'S THIRD "DO NOT READ" — no Amen after the prophets (the Amen of 306:37 refused); THE ENGLISH MISALIGNED — R. Dostai\'s teaching stands in this row\'s Hebrew but the export\'s English column carries it under 320:7 (the Hebrew governs the seat); the compile: no law (DV32-07). Fresh.')
srow(320, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"THEY HAVE ROUSED ME TO JEALOUSY WITH A NO-GOD, PROVOKED ME WITH THEIR VANITIES" (32:21) — A MAN MAY SERVE AN IMAGE, A THING THAT SEES HIM; BUT THEY SERVE A REFLECTION, AND NOT A REFLECTION ONLY BUT THE VAPOR (hevel) THAT RISES FROM THE POT — "PROVOKED ME WITH THEIR VAPORS". ({SP_(320, 7, "אבל", "הם", "עובדים", "לבבואה")} "but they serve a reflection"; {SP_(320, 7, "אלא", "להבל", "זה", "שעולה", "מן", "הקדרה")} "but the vapor that rises from the pot"): vanities read as steam (hevel both); the English of this row opens with 320:6\'s R. Dostai (the misalignment noted there); no law (DV32-07). Fresh.')
srow(320, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND I WILL ROUSE THEM TO JEALOUSY WITH A NO-PEOPLE (belo am)" — DO NOT READ "WITH A NO-PEOPLE" BUT "WITH A MIXED PEOPLE (belui am)": THESE ARE THEY WHO COME FROM AMONG THE NATIONS AND KINGDOMS AND DRIVE THEM FROM THEIR HOUSES. ({SP_(320, 8, "אלא", "בלוי", "עם")} "but: with a mixed people"; {SP_(320, 8, "ומוציאים", "אותם", "מתוך", "בתיהם")} "and drive them out of their houses"): the fourth "do not read" — the no-people the displaced; no law (DV32-07). Fresh.')
srow(320, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: THESE ARE THEY WHO COME FROM BARBARIA AND FROM MAURITANIA AND WALK NAKED IN THE MARKET — THERE IS NO MAN MORE DESPISED AND DEFECTIVE IN THE WORLD THAN ONE WHO WALKS NAKED IN THE MARKET. ({SP_(320, 9, "אלו", "הבאים", "מברבריא", "וממרטניא")} "these are they who come from Barbaria and from Mauritania"; {SP_(320, 9, "אלא", "המהלך", "ערום", "בשוק")} "than one who walks naked in the market"): the no-people named by their lands; no law (DV32-07). Fresh.')
srow(320, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"WITH A VILE NATION I WILL PROVOKE THEM" — THESE ARE THE SECTARIANS (minim): "THE VILE MAN HAS SAID IN HIS HEART: THERE IS NO GOD" (Psalm 14:1). ({SP_(320, 10, "אלו", "המינים")} "these are the sectarians"): the vile nation the deniers (the Writings\' seat cited, never read); no law (DV32-07). Fresh.')
srow(320, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR A FIRE IS KINDLED IN MY NOSTRIL (af)" (32:22) — WHEN PUNISHMENT GOES OUT FROM BEFORE ME IT GOES OUT ONLY IN ANGER (af); AND WHENCE THAT ANGER IS WITHIN GEHENNA? "AND BURNS TO THE DEPTHS OF SHEOL". ({SP_(320, 11, "אין", "יוצאה", "אלא", "באף")} "it goes out only in anger"; {SP_(320, 11, "ומנין", "אף", "בתוך", "גיהנם")} "and whence that anger is within Gehenna"): the nostril anger, the fire Gehenna\'s (Onkelos: an east wind from before Him — the measure); no law (DV32-07). Fresh.')
srow(320, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND DEVOURS THE EARTH WITH HER PRODUCE" — THIS IS THE LAND OF ISRAEL; "AND SETS ABLAZE THE FOUNDATIONS OF THE MOUNTAINS" — THIS IS JERUSALEM: "JERUSALEM, THE MOUNTAINS ARE ROUND ABOUT HER" (Psalm 125:2). ({SP_(320, 12, "זו", "ארץ", "ישראל")} "this is the land of Israel"; {SP_(320, 12, "זו", "ירושלם")} "this is Jerusalem"): the earth the land, the mountains Jerusalem (the Writings\' seat cited, never read); no law (DV32-07). Fresh.')
srow(320, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "AND DEVOURS THE EARTH WITH HER PRODUCE" — THIS IS THE WORLD AND ITS FULLNESS; "AND SETS ABLAZE THE FOUNDATIONS OF THE MOUNTAINS" — THESE ARE THE FOUR KINGDOMS: "AND BEHOLD, FOUR CHARIOTS" (Zechariah 6:1). ({SP_(320, 13, "זה", "העולם", "ומלואו")} "this is the world and its fullness"; {SP_(320, 13, "אלו", "ארבע", "מלכיות")} "these are the four kingdoms"): the last row of the piska — the fire on the kingdoms (the Prophets\' seat cited, never read); no law (DV32-07). Fresh.')
srow(321, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"I WILL HEAP EVILS UPON THEM" (32:23) — BEHOLD, I GATHER AND BRING UPON THEM ALL THE PUNISHMENTS TOGETHER AS ONE; ANOTHER WORD: I GATHER THEM ALL INTO A FORTRESS AND BRING UPON THEM ALL THE PUNISHMENTS AS ONE. The head row of piska 321 ({SP_(321, 1, "הריני", "מכניס", "ומביא", "עליהם", "כל", "הפרעניות", "כלם")} "behold, I gather and bring upon them all the punishments"; {SP_(321, 1, "לתוך", "מצודה")} "into a fortress"): the heaping as gathering (Onkelos: I will gather evils — the measure); no law (DV32-08). Fresh.')
srow(321, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: NOT "I WILL END (asof) EVILS UPON THEM" IS WRITTEN BUT "I WILL HEAP (aspeh)" — THAT ALL THE PUNISHMENTS BE SPENT AND THEY NOT SPENT; AND SO "MY ARROWS I WILL SPEND (akhalleh) ON THEM" — NOT "MY ARROWS SHALL CONSUME THEM" IS WRITTEN BUT "MY ARROWS I WILL SPEND ON THEM": MY ARROWS ARE SPENT AND THEY ARE NOT SPENT. ({SP_(321, 2, "שיהו", "כל", "פרעניות", "כלות", "והם", "אינם", "כלים")} "that all the punishments be spent and they not spent"; {SP_(321, 2, "חצי", "כלים", "והם", "אינם", "כלים")} "My arrows are spent and they are not spent"): THE ARROWS SPENT, ISRAEL NOT — the reading Sifrei 43:24 (outside) carried to chapter 11; the verb\'s form (akhalleh, I will spend, not yokhelu, they will consume) the ink the argument rests on; the compile: the punishment bounded, the people\'s survival a status (DV32-08). Fresh.')
srow(321, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "MY ARROWS I WILL SPEND ON THEM" — THESE ARE THE ARROWS OF FAMINE: "WHEN I SEND THE EVIL ARROWS OF FAMINE AGAINST THEM" (Ezekiel 5:16). ({SP_(321, 3, "אלו", "חצי", "רעב")} "these are the arrows of famine"): the arrows named (Onkelos: My plagues — the measure); the Prophets\' seat cited, never read; no law (DV32-08). Fresh.')
srow(321, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE WASTING OF HUNGER AND THE DEVOURING OF THE FIERY BOLT" (32:24) — THAT THEY BE WASTED WITH HUNGER AND CAST OUT IN THE STREETS: "AND THE PEOPLE TO WHOM THEY PROPHESY SHALL BE CAST OUT IN THE STREETS OF JERUSALEM" (Jeremiah 14:16). ({SP_(321, 4, "שיהיו", "מזאים", "ברעב", "ומשלכים", "בחוצות")} "that they be wasted with hunger and cast out in the streets"): THE SECOND MISPRINTED MARKER OF THE CHAPTER — the Hebrew row\'s marker reads 32:27 while its quoted words are 32:24\'s ("the wasting of hunger and the devouring of the fiery bolt"; the English cites 32:24) — the row seated at 32:24 by its own words (328\'s misprint the first, sitting 19\'s lesson 1); the Prophets\' seat cited, never read; no law (DV32-08). Fresh.')
srow(321, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND BITTER DESTRUCTION (ketev meriri)" — IN PASSING YOU LEARN THAT WHOEVER HAS A DEMON IN HIM FOAMS (merir). ({SP_(321, 5, "שכל", "מי", "שהשד", "בו", "הוא", "מריר")} "that whoever has a demon in him foams"): the demon of Onkelos\'s "evil spirits" (the measure) by the word\'s sound alone (the translator: "all we have is word-play"); no law (DV32-08). Fresh.')
srow(321, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE TEETH OF BEASTS" — DO NOT READ "THE TEETH OF BEASTS (behemot) I WILL SEND UPON THEM" BUT "THE TOOTH OF BESTIALITY (behamut) I WILL SEND UPON THEM": THAT THEY BE HEATED AND GO ROUND AFTER EVERY TRANSGRESSION. ({SP_(321, 6, "אל", "תהי", "קורא")} "do not read"; {SP_(321, 6, "שיהו", "מתחממים", "ומחזרים", "על", "כל", "עברות")} "that they be heated and go round after every transgression"): the fifth "do not read" — the beast\'s tooth an appetite; no law (DV32-08). Fresh.')
srow(321, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: THAT ONE OF THEM BE HEATED AND DRAW HIMSELF AND RAISE A GROWTH AND DIE OF IT; ANOTHER WORD: "THE TEETH OF BEASTS I WILL SEND UPON THEM" — THAT HIS OWN BEAST BITE HIM AND RAISE A GROWTH AND HE DIE OF IT; THEY SAID: IT HAPPENED THAT EWES BIT AND KILLED. ({SP_(321, 7, "שתהא", "בהמתו", "נושכתו")} "that his own beast bite him"; {SP_(321, 7, "שרחלים", "נושכים", "וממיתים")} "that ewes bit and killed"): the beast\'s tooth literal again — the ewe\'s bite (the English of this row repeats 321:8\'s text — a duplication in the export\'s English column); no law (DV32-08). Fresh.')
srow(321, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"WITH THE VENOM OF CRAWLING THINGS OF THE DUST" — THAT THEY BE DRAGGED IN THE DUST; RABBI SAYS: THESE ARE SERPENTS, WHOSE DOMINION IS ONLY IN THE DUST. ({SP_(321, 8, "שיהיו", "מוזחלין", "בעפר")} "that they be dragged in the dust"; {SP_(321, 8, "אלו", "עכנאים", "שאין", "שלטונם", "אלא", "בעפר")} "these are serpents, whose dominion is only in the dust"): the crawlers named serpents (Onkelos the same — the measure); no law (DV32-08). Fresh.')
srow(321, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"WITHOUT THE SWORD SHALL BEREAVE" (32:25) — FROM HERE THEY SAID: IN TIME OF WAR GATHER IN THE FOOT, IN TIME OF FAMINE SCATTER THE FOOT; "IF I GO OUT INTO THE FIELD, BEHOLD THE SLAIN OF THE SWORD, AND IF I ENTER THE CITY, BEHOLD THE SICKNESSES OF FAMINE" (Jeremiah 14:18), "HE THAT IS IN THE FIELD SHALL DIE BY THE SWORD, AND HE THAT IS IN THE CITY FAMINE AND PESTILENCE SHALL DEVOUR" (Ezekiel 7:15). ({SP_(321, 9, "בשעת", "מלחמה", "כנס", "את", "הרגל")} "in time of war gather in the foot"; {SP_(321, 9, "ובשעת", "רעב", "פזר", "את", "הרגל")} "in time of famine scatter the foot"): A RULE FROM THE VERSE — "from here they said": the sages\' counsel of war and famine (the Babylonian Talmud Bava Kamma 60b the testing shelf, cited); the compile: a rule of conduct with two conditions, the song its source — a candidate for the compile\'s case table (DV32-08); the Prophets\' seats cited, never read. Fresh.')
srow(321, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND IN THE CHAMBERS TERROR" — HE SAW THE SWORD COMING TO THE MARKET; COULD HE FLEE AND ESCAPE IT, THEN THE CHAMBERS OF HIS HEART BEAT ON HIM AND HE RAISES A GROWTH AND DIES OF IT. ({SP_(321, 10, "חדרי", "לבו", "נוקפים", "עליו")} "the chambers of his heart beat on him"): the chambers the heart\'s (Onkelos: the terror of death — the measure); no law (DV32-08). Fresh.')
srow(321, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "WITHOUT THE SWORD SHALL BEREAVE" — FOR WHAT THEY DID IN THE STREETS OF JERUSALEM: "FOR ACCORDING TO THE NUMBER OF YOUR CITIES WERE YOUR GODS, O JUDAH, AND ACCORDING TO THE NUMBER OF THE STREETS OF JERUSALEM YOU SET UP ALTARS TO THE SHAMEFUL THING" (Jeremiah 11:13); "AND IN THE CHAMBERS TERROR" — FOR WHAT THEY DID IN THE INNERMOST CHAMBERS: "HAVE YOU SEEN, SON OF MAN, WHAT THE ELDERS OF THE HOUSE OF ISRAEL DO IN THE DARK, EACH IN HIS CHAMBERS OF IMAGERY, SAYING: THE LORD DOES NOT SEE US" (Ezekiel 8:12). ({SP_(321, 11, "על", "מה", "שעשו", "בחוצות", "ירושלם")} "for what they did in the streets of Jerusalem"; {SP_(321, 11, "על", "מה", "שעשו", "בחדרי", "חדרים")} "for what they did in the innermost chambers"): the sword and the terror measure for measure — the street\'s sin and the chamber\'s; the Prophets\' seats cited, never read; no law (DV32-08). Fresh.')
srow(321, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'"BOTH YOUNG MAN AND VIRGIN" — THESE I MIGHT HAVE SPARED, BUT "THE SUCKLING WITH THE MAN OF GRAY HAIRS"? — "BOTH HUSBAND AND WIFE SHALL BE TAKEN, THE ELDER WITH HIM THAT IS FULL OF DAYS" (Jeremiah 6:11). ({SP_(321, 12, "הא", "ותרה", "לאלו")} "these I might have spared"; {SP_(321, 12, "אלא", "יונק", "עם", "איש", "שיבה")} "but the suckling with the man of gray hairs"): the four ages read as the sweep no one escapes; the Prophets\' seat cited, never read; no law (DV32-08). Fresh.')
srow(321, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "BOTH YOUNG MAN (bachur)" — YOU MADE ME STRETCH OUT MY HAND AGAINST MY CHOSEN (bechirai): "AND JOSHUA SON OF NUN, THE SERVANT OF MOSES FROM HIS YOUTH (mibchurav), ANSWERED" (Numbers 11:28). ({SP_(321, 13, "אתם", "גרמתם", "לי", "לשלוח", "יד", "בבחירי")} "you made Me stretch out My hand against My chosen"): the young man read as the chosen by the root (Numbers 11:28 the tape\'s own entry — a RUN CITATION); no law (DV32-08). Fresh.')
srow(321, 14, 'MATERIAL', f'"BOTH VIRGIN" — IT TEACHES THEY WERE CLEAN OF SIN AS A VIRGIN WHO NEVER TASTED SIN; "SUCKLING" — THEY SUCKED WORDS OF TORAH AS A SUCKLING SUCKS MILK FROM HIS MOTHER\'S BREASTS; "WITH THE MAN OF GRAY HAIRS (ish seivah)" — DO NOT READ "MAN OF GRAY HAIRS" BUT "MAN OF THE STUDY HOUSE (ish yeshivah)": ALL OF THEM FIT TO SIT IN THE STUDY HOUSE — "ALL OF THEM MIGHTY MEN, MAKERS OF WAR" (2 Kings 24:16): WHAT MIGHT DO MEN GOING INTO EXILE SHOW, AND WHAT WAR DO MEN BOUND IN FETTERS AND CHAINS MAKE? "MIGHTY" — MIGHTY IN TORAH ("BLESS THE LORD, HIS ANGELS, MIGHTY IN STRENGTH, WHO DO HIS WORD", Psalm 103:20); "MAKERS OF WAR" — WHO GAVE AND TOOK IN THE WAR OF TORAH ("THEREFORE IT IS SAID IN THE BOOK OF THE WARS OF THE LORD", Numbers 21:14); "AND THE CRAFTSMEN AND THE SMITHS A THOUSAND" (2 Kings 24:16) — CRAFTSMAN (charash): ONE SPEAKS AND ALL ARE SILENT (cheresh); SMITH (masger): ALL SIT BEFORE HIM AND LEARN FROM HIM — ONE OPENS AND ONE SHUTS, TO FULFIL "HE SHALL OPEN AND NONE SHALL SHUT, AND SHUT AND NONE SHALL OPEN" (Isaiah 22:22). ({SP_(321, 14, "מלמד", "שהיו", "מנקים", "מן", "החטא")} "it teaches they were clean of sin"; {SP_(321, 14, "אלא", "איש", "ישיבה")} "but: man of the study house"; {SP_(321, 14, "אלו", "גבורי", "תורה")} "these are the mighty in Torah"; {SP_(321, 14, "אחד", "פותח", "ואחד", "סוגר")} "one opens and one shuts"): THE EXILES OF JEHOIACHIN AS THE SAGES — the sixth "do not read" (yeshivah for seivah); 2 Kings 24:16\'s thousand craftsmen and smiths the study house\'s masters (the Prophets\' and the Writings\' seats cited, never read; Numbers 21:14 the tape\'s own entry — a RUN CITATION); the compile: no law (DV32-08). Fresh.')
srow(322, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"I SAID: I WOULD MAKE AN END OF THEM (af\'eihem)" (32:26) — I SAID IN MY ANGER (be\'appi): WHERE ARE THEY (ayeh hem)? The head row of piska 322 ({SP_(322, 1, "אמרתי", "באפי", "איה", "הם")} "I said in My anger: where are they"): the unique verb split into two words (anger and "where are they" — the translator names the assonance; Onkelos: My anger shall fall upon them — the measure); no law (DV32-09). Fresh.')
srow(322, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"I WOULD MAKE THEIR MEMORY CEASE FROM AMONG MEN (enosh)" — I SAID: LET THEM NOT BE IN THE WORLD; BUT WHAT SHALL I DO TO THEM? ({SP_(322, 2, "אמרתי", "לא", "יהיו", "בעולם")} "I said: let them not be in the world"; {SP_(322, 2, "אבל", "מה", "אעשה", "להם")} "but what shall I do to them"): the counterfactual opened — the seat that read this row at the Genesis ledger of Adam\'s line (enosh — the man of Genesis 5:6\'s name, the translator); no law (DV32-09). REREAD WHOLE (the Genesis ledger gen_14_adam_line_ledger\'s reading).')
srow(322, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"IF IT HAD NOT BEEN THE LORD WHO WAS ON OUR SIDE WHEN MAN (adam) ROSE UP AGAINST US" (Psalm 124:1-2). ({SP_(322, 3, "לולי", "ה", "שהיה", "לנו", "בקום", "עלינו", "אדם")} "if it had not been the LORD who was for us when man rose up against us"): the answer to "what shall I do" a Psalm verse alone; THE MARKER GARBLED in the export ("Deuteronomy 32" and "Psalms 124:1-2" run together in one parenthesis) — the row is the Psalm\'s (the Writings\' seat cited, never read); no law (DV32-09). Fresh.')
srow(322, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: I SAID IN MY ANGER, WHERE ARE THEY — "I WILL MAKE THEIR MEMORY CEASE FROM AMONG MEN", LET THEM NOT BE IN THE WORLD; BUT WHAT SHALL I DO — "EXCEPT THE LORD OF HOSTS HAD LEFT US A REMNANT" (Isaiah 1:9); ANOTHER WORD: "I SAID I WOULD MAKE AN END OF THEM" — WERE IT NOT AS IT SAYS "AND HE SAID HE WOULD DESTROY THEM, HAD NOT MOSES HIS CHOSEN STOOD IN THE BREACH BEFORE HIM" (Psalm 106:23). ({SP_(322, 4, "אבל", "מה", "אעשה")} "but what shall I do"; {SP_(322, 4, "לולי", "משה", "בחירו", "עמד", "בפרץ", "לפניו")} "had not Moses His chosen stood in the breach before Him"): THE "WERE IT NOT" CHAIN (lulei — 32:27\'s word) — the remnant and Moses in the breach (Exodus 32:11-14 the tape\'s own entry — a RUN CITATION; the Prophets\' and the Writings\' seats cited); the compile: the decree stayed by intercession — the argument of the calf on the tape (DV32-09). Fresh.')
srow(322, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"WERE IT NOT THAT I DREADED THE ENEMY\'S PROVOCATION" (32:27) — WHO CAUSED THEM TO BE PUNISHED BY THESE? THE ANGER OF THE NATIONS GATHERED IN THEIR BELLIES. ({SP_(322, 5, "מי", "גרם", "להם", "ליפרע", "מאלו")} "who caused them to be punished by these"; {SP_(322, 5, "כעס", "אמות", "שהיה", "כנוס", "בתוך", "מעיהם")} "the anger of the nations that was gathered in their bellies"): the enemy\'s anger gathered (Onkelos: the enemy\'s anger is gathered — the measure, the same reading); no law (DV32-09). Fresh.')
srow(322, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"I DREADED (agur)" — AGUR IS ONLY GATHERED: "THE WORDS OF AGUR SON OF JAKEH" (Proverbs 30:1), "LET DEATH SEIZE UPON THEM, LET THEM GO DOWN ALIVE TO SHEOL, FOR EVILS ARE GATHERED (bimguram) WITHIN THEM" (Psalm 55:16). ({SP_(322, 6, "אין", "אגור", "אלא", "כנוס")} "agur is only gathered"): the divine dread read away — the word means gathered (Onkelos the same); the Writings\' seats cited, never read; no law (DV32-09). Fresh.')
srow(322, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"LEST THEIR ADVERSARIES MISJUDGE (yenakkeru)" — IN THE HOUR OF ISRAEL\'S DISTRESS THE NATIONS OF THE WORLD ESTRANGE THEM AND MAKE AS IF THEY NEVER KNEW THEM; SO WE FIND THAT WHEN THEY SOUGHT TO FLEE NORTHWARD THEY WERE NOT GATHERED IN BUT HANDED OVER — "THUS SAYS THE LORD: FOR THREE TRANSGRESSIONS OF TYRE, AND FOR FOUR, I WILL NOT TURN IT BACK, BECAUSE THEY DELIVERED UP A WHOLE CAPTIVITY TO EDOM" (Amos 1:9); SOUTHWARD — "FOR THREE TRANSGRESSIONS OF GAZA … THEY CARRIED AWAY A WHOLE CAPTIVITY TO DELIVER THEM TO EDOM" (Amos 1:6); EASTWARD — "FOR THREE TRANSGRESSIONS OF DAMASCUS" (Amos 1:3); WESTWARD — "THE BURDEN UPON ARABIA: IN THE FOREST OF ARABIA SHALL YOU LODGE, O CARAVANS OF DEDANITES" (Isaiah 21:13). ({SP_(322, 7, "בשעת", "צרתם", "של", "ישראל")} "in the hour of Israel\'s distress"; {SP_(322, 7, "אמות", "העולם", "מנכרים", "אותם")} "the nations of the world estrange them"; {SP_(322, 7, "שבקשו", "לברח", "כלפי", "צפון")} "they sought to flee northward"): THE FOUR DIRECTIONS CLOSED — Amos 1\'s three cities and Isaiah\'s Arabia the four exits barred (the Prophets\' seats cited, never read); the verb yenakkeru read as estrange (n-k-r, the stranger); no law (DV32-09). Fresh.')
srow(322, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'IN THE HOUR OF ISRAEL\'S PROSPERITY THE NATIONS OF THE WORLD FLATTER THEM AND MAKE THEMSELVES AS BROTHERS — SO ESAU SAID TO JACOB "I HAVE ENOUGH, MY BROTHER, LET WHAT YOU HAVE BE YOURS" (Genesis 33:9), AND HIRAM TO SOLOMON "WHAT CITIES ARE THESE WHICH YOU HAVE GIVEN ME, MY BROTHER?" (1 Kings 9:13); "LEST THEY SAY: OUR HAND IS EXALTED AND NOT THE LORD HAS WROUGHT ALL THIS" — AS THOSE FOOLS SAID "HAVE WE NOT TAKEN KARNAIM BY OUR OWN STRENGTH?" (Amos 6:13). ({SP_(322, 8, "בשעת", "טובתם", "של", "ישראל")} "in the hour of Israel\'s prosperity"; {SP_(322, 8, "ועושים", "עצמם", "כאלו", "הם", "אחים")} "and make themselves as if they were brothers"; {SP_(322, 8, "כמו", "שאמרו", "אותם", "השוטים")} "as those fools said"): the brothers of good times (Genesis 33:9 the tape\'s own entry — a RUN CITATION; the Prophets\' seats cited) and THE ENEMY\'S BOAST quoted from Amos; no law (DV32-09). Fresh.')
srow(322, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR THEY ARE A NATION VOID OF COUNSEL" (32:28) — R. YEHUDAH EXPOUNDS IT OF ISRAEL, R. NEHEMIAH OF THE NATIONS OF THE WORLD. R. YEHUDAH OF ISRAEL: ISRAEL LOST THE GOOD COUNSEL GIVEN THEM, AND COUNSEL IS ONLY TORAH — "COUNSEL IS MINE, AND SOUND WISDOM" (Proverbs 8:14). ({SP_(322, 9, "רבי", "יהודה", "דורשו", "כלפי", "ישראל")} "R. Yehudah expounds it of Israel"; {SP_(322, 9, "ואין", "עצה", "אלא", "תורה")} "and counsel is only Torah"): THE NATION\'S IDENTITY DISPUTED — Israel or the nations (the Hebrew\'s goy both, the translator\'s note at 311:1); Onkelos leaves it open (the measure); the Writings\' seat cited, never read; no law (DV32-09). Fresh.')
srow(322, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THERE IS NO UNDERSTANDING IN THEM" — NOT ONE OF THEM LOOKS AND SAYS: YESTERDAY ONE OF US CHASED A THOUSAND OF THE NATIONS AND TWO PUT TEN THOUSAND TO FLIGHT, AND NOW ONE OF THE NATIONS CHASES A THOUSAND OF US AND TWO PUT TEN THOUSAND TO FLIGHT — "EXCEPT THEIR ROCK HAD SOLD THEM" (32:30). ({SP_(322, 10, "אמש", "אחד", "ממנו", "רודף", "מן", "האמות", "אלף")} "yesterday one of us chased a thousand of the nations"; {SP_(322, 10, "אם", "לא", "כי", "צורם", "מכרם")} "except their Rock had sold them"): THE JOINED THOUSAND READ BY THE SPINE — one, a thousand, two, ten thousand: four numbers, the proverb of 32:30 turned forward and back (the compile\'s guard against the parser\'s [1, 1002] confirmed by the shelf\'s own arithmetic — DV32-10); R. Yehudah\'s reading closed. Fresh.')
srow(322, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'R. NEHEMIAH EXPOUNDS IT OF THE NATIONS: THE NATIONS LOST THE SEVEN COMMANDMENTS I GAVE THEM. ({SP_(322, 11, "אבדו", "האמות", "שבע", "מצות", "שנתתי", "להם")} "the nations lost the seven commandments I gave them"): THE SEVEN COMMANDMENTS of the nations named in the spine (the Tosefta Avodah Zarah 8:4 the testing shelf, cited — the Noahide seven; the compile: a law set on the nations, its seat outside the tape\'s Israel ledger, cited); no law here (DV32-09). Fresh.')
srow(322, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THERE IS NO UNDERSTANDING IN THEM" — NOT ONE OF THEM LOOKS AND SAYS: NOW ONE OF US CHASES A THOUSAND OF ISRAEL AND TWO PUT TEN THOUSAND TO FLIGHT; IN THE DAYS OF THE MESSIAH ONE OF ISRAEL WILL CHASE A THOUSAND OF US AND TWO PUT TEN THOUSAND TO FLIGHT — "EXCEPT THEIR ROCK HAD SOLD THEM". IT HAPPENED IN THE WAR IN JUDAH THAT A DECURION RAN AFTER AN ISRAELITE ON HORSEBACK TO KILL HIM AND DID NOT OVERTAKE HIM; BEFORE HE OVERTOOK HIM A SNAKE CAME OUT AND BIT HIM ON THE HEEL; HE SAID TO HIM: DO NOT THINK TO SAY THAT BECAUSE WE ARE MIGHTY THEY WERE GIVEN INTO OUR HAND — "EXCEPT THEIR ROCK HAD SOLD THEM". ({SP_(322, 12, "לימות", "המשיח", "אחד", "מישראל", "רודף", "ממנו", "אלף")} "in the days of the Messiah one of Israel will chase a thousand of us"; {SP_(322, 12, "מעשה", "בפולמוס", "שביהודה")} "it happened in the war in Judah"; {SP_(322, 12, "יצא", "נחש", "ונשך", "לו", "על", "עקבו")} "a snake came out and bit him on the heel"): the last row of the piska — R. Nehemiah\'s reading closed by the Roman\'s own confession (the war in Judah — Bar Kokhba\'s, the translator); 32:30\'s proverb the third time in the piska; no law (DV32-09, DV32-10). Fresh.')
